/-!
# Witness data for `DoubleLanding`

One line per configuration `(x, i, y, j)` of a copy of `X15` whose exits `x < y` (in
`{4, 6, 9}`) land on the positions `i`, `j` of one 13-vertex window, outside the ten legal
configurations.  Vertices of the 28-vertex configuration graph are `0 … 14` (`X15`) and
`15 … 27` (the window `p₀ … p₁₂`); every number `v` is written as `Char.ofNat (48 + v)`.
A line is the four configuration characters, then `C` followed by a cycle of length 4, 8 or
16, or `P` followed by two induced 13-vertex paths (13 + 13 characters).  Every line is
re-checked by `native_decide` in `DoubleLanding`.
-/

